From af6e20de4903ea5300a9b6f696476d4006ff5358 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JohnnyC96 <54557697+JohnnyC96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:16:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Runtime: upscale/window settings, pnach memory patches, game
 serial

Three start-up features for an external GPU GS (high resolution,
widescreen, texture packs):

1. Settings (ps2_game_source): upscale = 1..8 (an external GPU GS's
   render resolution multiplier; unset = 1) and window = <W>x<H> (the
   host window at start-up, at least 320x224; unset = the built-in size).
   Other values are bad lines that leave them unset. InitWindow uses it.

2. pnach (new ps2_pnach.h/.cpp): every *.pnach in <mods>/<serial>/
   (folder in any case, files in name order) is read before the window
   opens. patch=<place>,EE,<addr>,<type>,<value> with byte/short/word or
   extended 0/1/2 writes; place 0 = once at boot, 1 = every vsync,
   2 = both (PCSX2's semantics); gsaspectratio=4:3|16:9. Comments,
   [sections], gametitle/description/author/comment are ignored; other
   CPUs, types, conditional extended codes, unaligned and malformed
   lines are skipped with "[pnach] <file> line N: <reason>".
   After the ELF load, writes inside recompiled code (the boot ELF's
   function table range and every registered guest module) are dropped
   with one line each: code is compiled ahead of time, so they need a
   recompile. The rest are applied at boot (PS2Runtime::applyPnachAtBoot)
   and continuous ones at every VBlankStart (EeScheduler).
   gsaspectratio=16:9 widens the built-in window to 16:9 at the same
   height; activePnach().aspect is there for the external GS.

3. activeGameSerial(): the resolved game's serial, set by main once the
   game source is known, for an external GS's texture replacement
   (<textures>/<serial>/replacements). The textures log line now says
   the textures are loaded by an external GS that supports them.

Tests (ps2x): settings upscale/window (valid, X in any case, quoted,
five bad lines, empty clears); pnach parse (all write forms, places,
aspect; nine rejected lines with reasons), code-range drop and boot /
vsync apply (a value written back by the game is re-applied; writes past
RAM ignored), folder lookup (case, order, non-.pnach ignored, other
serial, no mods root); active serial set/clear. Without this patch they
do not compile (no upscale/window fields, no ps2_pnach.h, no
activeGameSerial).
